# Floply — environment variables.
#
# Copy to `.env`. Everything here is shown with its default and is optional, except the AWS
# credentials, so the shortest useful .env is just those two lines.
#
# `pnpm dev` and `pnpm preview` load `.env` through `node --env-file-if-exists`. Vite's own
# .env handling is not sufficient: it populates `import.meta.env` and SvelteKit's `$env/*`,
# but the AWS SDK reads `process.env`. The production server loads nothing — `node
# build/index.js` reads the real environment, so export the vars or run it with
# `node --env-file=.env build/index.js`.
#
# Why the guards and thresholds are set where they are: lib/server/pricing.ts. Overview of
# the common settings: README.md.


# -- AWS credentials — required, unless FLOPLY_PRICING_FIXTURE=1 ---------------
#
# Read-only access suffices, and grants nothing over your account's data:
#   pricing:GetProducts, ec2:DescribeInstanceTypes, ec2:DescribeInstanceTypeOfferings
#
# Resolved through the standard AWS SDK chain, so to use ~/.aws, AWS_PROFILE, or an
# instance/task role, leave these commented out. Setting them to a placeholder does not fall
# back to that chain — it overrides it and fails to authenticate, surfacing as AuthFailure.
# Substitute real values; the angle brackets are not literal.
#AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<your-access-key-id>
#AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<your-secret-access-key>

# Temporary or assumed-role credentials only.
#AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# Instead of the two keys above.
#AWS_PROFILE=default


# -- Pricing: regions ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# FLOPLY_DEFAULT_REGION must be one of FLOPLY_AWS_REGIONS, and FLOPLY_PRICING_API_REGION must
# be us-east-1, eu-central-1, or ap-south-1 — the only endpoints serving the Price List API,
# and unrelated to the region being priced. Either one violated throws on the first request.
#FLOPLY_AWS_REGIONS=us-east-1,us-west-2,eu-west-1,eu-central-1,ap-northeast-1,ap-south-1
#FLOPLY_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
#FLOPLY_PRICING_API_REGION=us-east-1

# Region for the one region-agnostic DescribeInstanceTypes call.
#FLOPLY_SPECS_REGION=us-east-1


# -- Pricing: freshness and cache ----------------------------------------------
#
# Refresh thresholds in days, never expiry: past them the cached numbers are still served,
# flagged stale in the UI, and refreshed off the render path.
#FLOPLY_PRICING_TTL_DAYS=30
#FLOPLY_SPECS_TTL_DAYS=90

# Falls back to $XDG_CACHE_HOME/floply, then ~/.cache/floply, then nothing persists. In
# Docker, mount a volume over /app/.cache/floply or a container replacement drops the cache
# the app relies on during an AWS outage.
#FLOPLY_CACHE_DIR=.cache/floply


# -- Pricing: discovery and guards ---------------------------------------------
#
# Instance families eligible for discovery, and the minimum GPUs to offer one. Unconstrained,
# DescribeInstanceTypes returns 60+ NVIDIA types including single-GPU sizes.
#FLOPLY_INSTANCE_FAMILY_ALLOWLIST=p
#FLOPLY_DISCOVER_MIN_GPUS=4

# Reject a fetched price this many times off the cached one, and refuse to overwrite a cache
# entry with a fetch returning fewer instances than this. Rejected values fall back to the
# cached price and surface as warnings, never dropped silently.
#FLOPLY_PRICING_MAX_DRIFT=4
#FLOPLY_PRICING_MIN_INSTANCES=3

# Per-request AWS timeout, and the wait after a failed background refresh before retrying.
#FLOPLY_PRICING_TIMEOUT_S=10
#FLOPLY_PRICING_RETRY_BACKOFF_S=900


# -- Fixture mode (development and CI) -----------------------------------------
#
# Serve frozen fixture prices instead of calling AWS. Runs with no credentials, and is what
# the e2e suite uses to assert exact dollar figures.
#
# Opt-in only, never a fallback: leave it unset in production, so a misconfigured deployment
# shows "pricing unavailable" rather than quietly serving numbers that look real and are not.
#FLOPLY_PRICING_FIXTURE=1


# -- Analytics (optional) ------------------------------------------------------
#
# Umami, cookieless. Injected only when both are set, and read at request time so one image
# can be deployed to several environments.
#UMAMI_URL=https://analytics.example.com/script.js
#UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


# -- Server — read by @sveltejs/adapter-node, not by application code ----------
#
# ORIGIN and the header vars are needed only behind a reverse proxy, so redirects and CSRF
# checks resolve against the public URL.
#PORT=3000
#HOST=0.0.0.0
#ORIGIN=https://floply.example.com
#PROTOCOL_HEADER=x-forwarded-proto
#HOST_HEADER=x-forwarded-host
#ADDRESS_HEADER=x-forwarded-for
#XFF_DEPTH=1
#BODY_SIZE_LIMIT=512K
